# Check out LF everywhere, including on Windows.
#
# Two things in this repository break on CRLF, and both broke silently until CI
# ran on a Windows runner:
#
#   `vibrev-skills`' frontmatter parser opens SKILL.md with
#   `strip_prefix("---\n")`, which returns None against `---\r\n`. The build
#   script then fails with "frontmatter has no `name:`" on a file that has one.
#
#   The e2e scripts are bash. A CRLF shebang line is not a shebang.
#
# Nothing tracked here is binary — the compiled fixtures and IDA databases are
# generated and ignored — so a blanket rule is safe. The explicit binary lines
# below exist so that an .i64 committed by accident is not mangled on top of
# being committed by accident.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.i64 binary
*.idb binary
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
